WEBVTT

00:10.570 --> 00:12.690
Thank goodness she didn't lock the base.

00:12.690 --> 00:13.820
Do you sense anyone nearby?

00:13.820 --> 00:15.450
No. There is no one.

00:16.370 --> 00:18.680
I will go search for the items we need.

00:23.960 --> 00:27.130
As long as everything goes well, 
you'll be able to take your time reading.

00:27.130 --> 00:28.330
You are right...

00:41.140 --> 00:48.860
Spice and Wolf

02:01.380 --> 02:02.500
Mr. Lawrence!

02:03.600 --> 02:07.600
<b>Episode 25
Miracle's Path and
Journey's Continuation</b>

02:04.200 --> 02:04.970
Here!

02:04.970 --> 02:07.400
Now we just need to find the right time.

02:09.390 --> 02:10.650
How are things going?

02:11.010 --> 02:12.390
Can you tell what they're saying?

02:15.020 --> 02:17.150
They are demanding money.

02:17.480 --> 02:18.150
Oh...

02:20.010 --> 02:23.090
He's the one who planned to trap us.

02:23.090 --> 02:25.300
Hey! What the hell're you doing?!

02:25.300 --> 02:26.840
That's...

02:27.890 --> 02:31.420
The bread baker. He complains to me the most.

02:33.490 --> 02:35.080
It is over.

02:35.080 --> 02:37.590
They have received their final ultimatum.

02:48.140 --> 02:52.230
"All will be fine if you light this on fire 
and accept the true teachings."

02:52.230 --> 02:55.560
"Otherwise, we shall declare 
your village pagan."

02:56.610 --> 02:59.400
Humans always depend 
on others when they are in trouble.

03:00.010 --> 03:03.720
Yet, there have been times when 
I have depended on humans as well.

03:03.720 --> 03:05.310
What shall we do?

03:08.000 --> 03:10.650
As a servant of the true faith,

03:10.650 --> 03:12.750
I cannot abandon my village.

03:17.410 --> 03:18.920
So, let us go forth.

03:32.290 --> 03:33.240
Elsa!

03:34.700 --> 03:36.840
Elsa! Why?!

03:36.840 --> 03:38.720
I'm sorry, Ms. Iima.

03:38.720 --> 03:40.170
Well, well.

03:40.170 --> 03:42.700
If it isn't Ms. Elsa, 
the successor of Father Franz.

03:42.700 --> 03:45.540
It has been a long time, Bishop Mendez.

03:45.540 --> 03:47.870
I was told that you ran away.

03:47.870 --> 03:50.660
Was your guilt too heavy 
to bear on your conscience?

03:50.660 --> 03:54.120
God is always forgiving to those 
who have committed sins.

03:55.570 --> 03:59.790
The people of Enberch, who follow the true 
faith, have been suffering under this curse,

03:59.790 --> 04:03.260
while the people of Tereo are unaffected.

04:05.010 --> 04:09.850
They are obviously under the
protection of an evil pagan god.

04:10.360 --> 04:15.690
We will rebuild a new and proper 
holy church of the true faith here.

04:15.690 --> 04:23.010
The false servant of God is a poisonous
 evil snake in sheep's clothing

04:23.010 --> 04:25.990
that will face the judgment 
of our most righteous God.

04:27.080 --> 04:28.830
That is not necessary.

04:29.140 --> 04:32.330
It is true that my faith has wavered at times.

04:32.690 --> 04:37.040
However, God has graciously 
shown me the true path.

04:37.510 --> 04:40.340
I have met one of His divine messengers!

04:46.220 --> 04:50.940
The fact that you claim to have met a divine 
messenger so easily is proof of your heresy!

04:50.940 --> 04:54.560
If I am wrong, bring proof before me!

04:55.860 --> 04:58.190
Allow me to show you if you have doubts!

05:03.180 --> 05:04.860
Let them through.

05:05.940 --> 05:08.990
Father Franz was a talented man.

05:08.990 --> 05:12.580
He was an admirable servant of God.

05:12.580 --> 05:16.750
However, he should have acted 
in accordance with the will of the Church.

05:16.750 --> 05:20.750
It also seems like he failed 
to raise a proper successor.

05:20.750 --> 05:24.590
The worship of the serpent god, 
Truyeo, is indeed a mistake.

05:25.030 --> 05:28.590
However, the mistake itself 
is not completely off the mark.

05:31.510 --> 05:34.480
I believe that Truyeo itself

05:36.190 --> 05:39.520
is one of God's miracles.

05:40.910 --> 05:45.280
She neither confirmed nor 
denied Truyeo. A clever move.

05:45.280 --> 05:49.030
The words of men easily stray from the truth.

05:49.030 --> 05:52.480
How can you be sure that they 
were not the whispers of the devil?

05:52.480 --> 05:55.810
The divine messenger promised to reveal a sign,

05:55.810 --> 06:00.420
to guide the lost lambs of God 
onto the true path.

06:01.610 --> 06:03.760
That God would show 
his power to someone like...

06:04.380 --> 06:05.840
Th-The wheat!

06:34.900 --> 06:37.920
God! It's a miracle of God!

06:37.920 --> 06:39.000
God!

06:40.830 --> 06:42.580
Th-That's...

06:42.580 --> 06:45.000
Look! The wheat on that carriage!

06:45.000 --> 06:47.590
Only the wheat there grew no ears!

06:57.540 --> 07:00.080
God has shown us the true path.

07:00.080 --> 07:02.870
I-Impossible. This...

07:03.650 --> 07:09.600
Bishop Mendez, I would like you to confirm 
that this is not an act of the devil.

07:09.600 --> 07:11.550
H-How?

07:13.020 --> 07:14.240
With this.

07:14.530 --> 07:17.410
Please bless this chalice.

07:17.410 --> 07:21.050
Once you have done so, 
Evan, who mills the wheat of this village,

07:21.050 --> 07:23.750
will prove God's righteousness 
with his own body.

07:23.750 --> 07:26.540
Wh-What exactly do you plan 
to prove with this?

07:26.540 --> 07:30.340
Even the poor may be baptized in God's name.

07:30.340 --> 07:34.470
Please cleanse this chalice 
with your own hands.

07:39.070 --> 07:40.100
Please.

07:49.590 --> 07:54.160
Water poured by the bishop is holy 
and this chalice has been blessed.

07:54.560 --> 07:57.030
Take this chalice to him there.

08:00.550 --> 08:02.380
Please watch closely.

08:24.020 --> 08:29.320
With this, except for one, 
he has collected flour from every cart.

08:44.760 --> 08:50.880
This is the truth of God's miracle that 
the divine messenger has revealed to us.

08:52.580 --> 08:57.640
If this miracle is false, you should surely 
be able to demonstrate a true one.

08:58.590 --> 09:05.160
Bishop Mendez. 
If we are wrong, you must correct us.

09:06.600 --> 09:08.730
Will you drink this water?

09:13.250 --> 09:17.860
V-Very well. This is a miracle. A true miracle.

09:17.860 --> 09:20.310
Then, the church of this village?

09:22.020 --> 09:25.070
Legitimate. It is a legitimate church.

09:25.070 --> 09:27.550
Then, please put that in writing.

09:46.780 --> 09:48.050
Father...

09:48.050 --> 09:49.270
Thank you.

09:52.930 --> 09:54.540
You look envious.

09:54.540 --> 09:56.570
Yeah, I am.

09:56.990 --> 09:59.660
This time, we only worked behind the scenes.

10:01.270 --> 10:06.580
However, the issue of money still has 
not been resolved. Is that not your job?

10:06.580 --> 10:07.810
You're right.

10:07.810 --> 10:11.130
But I can't believe how completely 
the tables have turned...

10:17.570 --> 10:20.340
Yes, I think I can make things work.

10:22.520 --> 10:23.280
What is it?

10:23.280 --> 10:27.220
Are you sure you are 
not actually a wolf yourself?

10:32.100 --> 10:33.260
Mr. Riendott.

10:34.010 --> 10:35.700
Please wait a moment.

10:39.770 --> 10:42.910
While they settle the matters of religion,

10:43.280 --> 10:45.740
we still need to settle matters of money.

10:49.820 --> 10:51.660
So, Mr. Riendott.

10:51.660 --> 10:52.710
Y-Yes!

10:53.070 --> 10:56.470
I've been asked to handle 
all the negotiations of coin.

10:56.980 --> 10:59.190
I am sure the villagers have no objections?

11:00.470 --> 11:02.890
We can't go against the village head...

11:03.410 --> 11:05.180
That's how it is.

11:05.180 --> 11:08.850
Then, let's start with the greatest demand.

11:09.430 --> 11:11.480
We'd like you to keep the wheat.

11:15.450 --> 11:16.690
Th-That's impossible!

11:16.690 --> 11:17.790
Why?

11:17.790 --> 11:21.070
Wh-Why? There's been a death!

11:21.070 --> 11:24.610
My shop's reputation has already been damaged!

11:24.610 --> 11:25.950
Besides! Besides!

11:25.950 --> 11:29.790
Our contract with Father Franz states that

11:29.790 --> 11:33.250
the wheat can all be returned 
if Ridelius' Hellfire is found in it.

11:33.560 --> 11:34.580
I understand.

11:34.580 --> 11:38.100
Then, what's the price for 
accepting the returned wheat?

11:40.010 --> 11:41.300
T-Two hundred Ri...

11:41.300 --> 11:42.550
Don't be ridiculous!

11:44.260 --> 11:47.770
That's the exact same price you bought it at!

11:47.770 --> 11:51.520
Th-Th-Th-Then, one hundred and ninety-five...

11:51.520 --> 11:53.380
You're still talking nonsense!

11:53.380 --> 11:54.350
Now, now.

11:54.720 --> 11:55.790
Mr. Riendott.

11:55.790 --> 12:00.570
Won't it be bad for you if 
another miracle were to happen?

12:00.570 --> 12:01.640
Wha?!

12:01.640 --> 12:04.090
The story of poisonous wheat is actually—

12:04.090 --> 12:07.970
No! No! I understand! I understand!

12:07.970 --> 12:10.950
One hundred and six...

12:10.950 --> 12:16.630
No, fif... f-forty...

12:20.060 --> 12:22.260
Then, let's go with that.

12:22.260 --> 12:24.050
Everyone here is bearing witness.

12:27.270 --> 12:28.920
By the way, Mr. Riendott.

12:29.350 --> 12:32.850
Would you like to buy back 
the wheat you've returned?

12:34.700 --> 12:35.940
I understand.

12:35.940 --> 12:38.290
However, the people of this village don't have

12:38.290 --> 12:40.230
enough cash on hand to pay 
for the returned wheat.

12:40.230 --> 12:42.470
Even with the lowered cost, 
they still lack the funds.

12:43.930 --> 12:45.780
So, I have a proposal.

12:46.840 --> 12:48.290
It's a simple one.

12:48.290 --> 12:54.240
I'd like you to persuade the bishop to allow 
the village to sell wheat under his name.

12:54.240 --> 12:54.920
Huh?

12:55.920 --> 13:01.180
If you plan to sell this wheat to other 
businesses, I think you should give up...

13:01.180 --> 13:03.210
I am fully aware of that.

13:03.210 --> 13:06.280
So, can you do this favor for us?

13:06.280 --> 13:08.890
I th-think I can...

13:08.890 --> 13:09.970
Then, one more thing.

13:09.970 --> 13:15.380
It's possible that the people of Enberch 
will cause trouble in my business.

13:15.380 --> 13:18.940
I'd like you to be my ally in that case.

13:20.010 --> 13:22.570
You can't possibly be thinking of making bread?

13:22.570 --> 13:26.200
No, the bakers would definitely 
not allow such a thing. Don't worry.

13:26.200 --> 13:28.260
Wh-What in the world...

13:28.260 --> 13:33.290
Now, now. We'll return the money 
once that business goes well.

13:33.290 --> 13:35.810
No, I can't accept such a condition...

13:35.810 --> 13:37.960
Of course, I'm not saying you wait for free.

13:38.330 --> 13:41.090
I'm adding on an extremely 
attractive condition.

13:43.060 --> 13:46.340
Why don't we dissolve the contract 
created by Father Franz?

13:48.340 --> 13:50.010
Hey! You can't decide that on your own!

13:50.010 --> 13:52.120
Even if the village head 
left the negotiations to you!

13:52.120 --> 13:54.990
But, as long as the contract exists,

13:54.990 --> 13:57.810
the town of Enberch 
will continue to resent you.

14:00.120 --> 14:01.480
Am I right?

14:02.930 --> 14:05.490
This contract was abnormal from to begin with.

14:06.060 --> 14:08.990
Contracts should be made to benefit both sides.

14:08.990 --> 14:11.340
That's business.

14:12.780 --> 14:15.950
What do you think? Will you do as I request?

14:15.950 --> 14:16.760
Hey!

14:16.760 --> 14:17.530
But...

14:17.530 --> 14:21.130
If Mr. Riendott and Bishop Mendez 
are willing to be on our side,

14:21.130 --> 14:25.050
I can suggest a wonderful 
business idea to this village.

14:28.410 --> 14:30.330
What are you...

14:30.330 --> 14:34.090
Though, we'll need some 
cooperation from the baker.

14:35.140 --> 14:38.390
Also, can you prepare some eggs and butter?

14:38.390 --> 14:40.100
Honey, too, if possible.

14:41.540 --> 14:44.960
It seems this proposal 
will result in something delicious.

14:52.410 --> 14:54.700
Don't eat while you're reading.

14:56.300 --> 14:58.480
Don't scatter crumbs everywhere.

14:58.480 --> 15:01.320
Sure, sure. I got it.

15:05.130 --> 15:08.620
These "biscuit" things are delicious.

15:09.550 --> 15:13.430
They are selling well in Enberch 
as a Tereo specialty.

15:13.430 --> 15:20.100
At this rate, not only will we be able to return the money, but turn a profit as well.

15:20.610 --> 15:24.940
Who would have guessed that the flat bread 
you talked about would be this delicious.

15:24.940 --> 15:27.940
Yeah. They're common in the south 
but unknown around here,

15:27.940 --> 15:31.910
so I thought it would be good business.

15:31.910 --> 15:33.570
Even though wheat is used,

15:33.570 --> 15:36.370
it's baked before the blessing 
of the bread-leavening spirits.

15:36.370 --> 15:40.540
It looks nothing like bread, so the bread 
bakers have no reason to complain.

15:40.920 --> 15:42.750
Well, even if something happens,

15:42.750 --> 15:46.590
we've made a profit-sharing contract 
with Riendott and Bishop Mendez.

15:46.590 --> 15:48.130
I'm sure they'll handle it.

15:48.130 --> 15:50.290
Though, it was difficult to go through

15:50.290 --> 15:53.430
all the bags of wheat 
to confirm the lack of poison...

15:54.290 --> 15:56.260
Well, we should go soon.

15:56.260 --> 15:58.090
Huh? Already?

16:01.310 --> 16:03.480
Well, I guess we should.

16:09.240 --> 16:12.030
Please come visit again whenever 
you wish to read the books.

16:12.030 --> 16:14.090
Then, make sure...

16:16.870 --> 16:19.240
to have plenty of biscuits prepared when I do.

16:19.630 --> 16:20.830
Of course.

16:20.830 --> 16:22.750
I'll mill a mountain of flour for you!

16:22.750 --> 16:25.740
I see. Then I'll make sure 
to turn a huge profit

16:25.740 --> 16:28.160
with that flour the next time we visit.

16:30.740 --> 16:31.940
That's right.

16:31.940 --> 16:35.340
The attitude of the villagers 
has changed since then.

16:35.340 --> 16:39.970
I've been chosen to take care 
of our negotiations with Enberch.

16:39.970 --> 16:42.020
Oh? That's amazing.

16:42.020 --> 16:46.230
Lately, there have been more 
people stopping by the church.

16:46.230 --> 16:50.690
Even so, Lord Truyeo is still way more popular.

16:51.040 --> 16:53.150
True. But...

16:53.480 --> 16:58.810
I want to continue my duty 
as a servant of God here in this village.

17:00.340 --> 17:03.450
Ms. Elsa, you asked me a question once before.

17:03.860 --> 17:06.210
Have you found your answer?

17:06.210 --> 17:06.920
Yes.

17:07.310 --> 17:11.670
You told me that my father was not wrong.

17:12.320 --> 17:15.380
I thought over it for a long time.

17:15.760 --> 17:19.880
Why did my father collect stories 
about pagan gods?

17:20.780 --> 17:27.930
I believe that he wanted to confirm 
the existence of pagan gods

17:27.930 --> 17:29.980
to confirm the existence of God.

17:29.980 --> 17:32.420
Yes. I agree.

17:32.420 --> 17:37.680
That is the very reason that I believe 
it isn't good for the church of Enberch

17:37.680 --> 17:40.180
to refute the existence of Truyeo.

17:40.180 --> 17:44.520
Well, all of this was 
thanks to the miracle I created.

17:44.980 --> 17:50.920
If a creature like you 
can create such a grand miracle,

17:50.920 --> 17:57.440
it is clear that our God could easily 
create all living things in this world.

17:59.030 --> 18:04.060
And, if Truyeo can create 
miracles as grand as yours...

18:04.520 --> 18:08.720
Well, the people of this village 
have a good eye...

18:09.750 --> 18:11.470
That's all there is to it.

18:26.230 --> 18:27.680
Mr. Lawrence.

18:34.060 --> 18:36.710
Are you continuing your travels?

18:36.710 --> 18:39.220
You should have said something.

18:39.220 --> 18:41.560
Thank you for taking care of us until now.

18:41.560 --> 18:42.680
Not at all.

18:43.000 --> 18:46.680
Our village was saved thanks to your help.

18:46.680 --> 18:49.660
Elsa and Evan, too.

18:55.430 --> 18:58.170
Thank you!

18:59.590 --> 19:01.110
Then, farewell.

19:17.820 --> 19:22.390
Travelers don't leave behind regrets 
in a village, but good memories.

19:41.810 --> 19:43.130
Farewell!

19:56.750 --> 19:59.280
May you be blessed by God's grace.

20:01.150 --> 20:05.260
Just like the apples, should we have 
all your meals be biscuits?

20:05.260 --> 20:08.180
Who was the one that sniffed out 
the poison and created a miracle?

20:08.180 --> 20:12.350
Without me, you would have been 
stripped naked and burned at the stake.

20:12.350 --> 20:14.690
That's that. This is this.

20:15.120 --> 20:18.450
Even so, we truly faced calamity this time.

20:18.450 --> 20:22.990
Well, we were able to sell our wheat 
at a decent price. We still made a profit.

20:22.990 --> 20:25.030
That is all you ever care about.

20:25.530 --> 20:31.520
My hopes were not fully met 
this time, but I gained enough.

20:31.520 --> 20:33.210
I believe it was worth the effort.

20:36.260 --> 20:39.330
So, where are we going next?

20:39.330 --> 20:43.630
Lenos. The town 
you personally left a legend in.

20:43.630 --> 20:45.820
Oh, is that right?

20:49.630 --> 20:52.700
Do not make such a greedy face.

20:52.700 --> 20:54.490
I've already eaten plenty!

20:56.180 --> 20:58.520
Yet, you still have a greedy look to you.

21:05.030 --> 21:06.700
Wh-What?

21:06.700 --> 21:08.100
It is nothing.

21:11.770 --> 21:12.370
Hey.

21:12.750 --> 21:13.430
Hm?

21:14.030 --> 21:16.660
I heard of a good business deal...

21:16.660 --> 21:17.870
Oh?

21:18.460 --> 21:19.290
But...

21:21.560 --> 21:23.760
it's a bit out of the way.

21:25.450 --> 21:28.950
Then, my travels with you 
will grow ever longer.

21:28.950 --> 21:32.520
It cannot be helped. 
I suppose I can accompany you.

21:33.550 --> 21:34.360
So?

21:40.530 --> 21:42.500
What business is to be had?

23:07.460 --> 23:10.010
Well, that is enough for today.

23:10.010 --> 23:11.310
What?!

23:11.310 --> 23:12.320
It is late.

23:12.860 --> 23:14.490
Time for you to sleep.

23:14.490 --> 23:17.690
But I still want to hear more!

23:17.690 --> 23:19.330
There's more, isn't there?

23:19.610 --> 23:24.020
The secret to a good journey 
is to take your time and enjoy it.

23:24.020 --> 23:25.300
But...

23:26.090 --> 23:27.530
He's home!

23:29.470 --> 23:31.970
Hey, you little fool! Where are you going?

23:32.240 --> 23:34.180
I have to welcome him home!

23:34.180 --> 23:37.600
Tell me more tomorrow! It's a promise!

23:39.350 --> 23:40.980
Fine, fine.

23:42.870 --> 23:46.700
Of course, the story is far from finished...
